# Public pages stay accurate

The home page, privacy policy, and terms live in this repository. A change that makes any sentence on them false must update those files in the same change.

- Home: `docs/index.html`
- Privacy: `docs/privacy.html`
- Terms: `docs/terms.html`

The same pages are also static files on the personal site, because an existing OAuth consent screen may still point at them. Keep those copies in sync when the repo pages change. Do not host these pages on GitHub Pages. Do not link them from the site navigation, home page, or project list.

- Home: `D:\Upwork\mehdimamas.dev\public\gmail-otp-copier\index.html` → https://mehdimamas.dev/gmail-otp-copier/
- Privacy: `D:\Upwork\mehdimamas.dev\public\gmail-otp-copier\privacy.html` → https://mehdimamas.dev/gmail-otp-copier/privacy/
- Terms: `D:\Upwork\mehdimamas.dev\public\gmail-otp-copier\terms.html` → https://mehdimamas.dev/gmail-otp-copier/terms/

They are static files in `public/`, outside the site layout. Leave the rewrites in `D:\Upwork\mehdimamas.dev\next.config.mjs` so the clean URLs keep serving the HTML files.

## Update the pages when a change affects

- OAuth scopes, Google APIs called, or permissions in `wxt.config.ts`
- What is read from Gmail, what is stored, where it is stored, or how long it is kept (`lib/storage.ts`, `lib/types.ts`, `lib/gmail.ts`, `lib/auth.ts`)
- Whether mail, codes, or tokens leave the browser
- Auto-fill, auto-copy, notifications, clipboard, or the fill chip
- Who the app is, the license, or the support contact

Leave the pages alone for refactors, tests, and styling that do not change those facts.

## How to edit them

- Describe only what the code does. Do not add data uses the extension does not have.
- On the privacy and terms pages, set "Last updated" to today's date when the text changes.
- Keep the Google API Services User Data Policy Limited Use sentence in the privacy policy.
- If a README link or URL for these pages is wrong, fix it too.
- Include the page edits in the same commit when the user asks to commit. Do not commit or push only to refresh the site unless they asked to publish.
